    [Doc] Clarify GLM-5 discontinuation and align GLM-5.1 deployment examples (#18552)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Clarify that GLM-5 is discontinued starting with vLLM Ascend v0.30.0 and
    make the deployment examples specific to GLM-5.1. The guide currently
    combines GLM-5 and GLM-5.1, lists GLM-5 weights and serves requests
    under the `glm-5` alias even in GLM-5.1 examples.
    
    - Keep the GLM-5 & GLM-5.1 page and navigation title, add the
    discontinuation notice as the first introduction paragraph, and list the
    supported GLM-5.1 model in the support matrix. Keep the existing file
    URL.
    - Remove the two GLM-5 weight entries and retain the four existing
    GLM-5.1 weight entries.
    - Use GLM-5.1 throughout the model description, checkpoint paths,
    deployment commands, request/response examples and FAQ. All serving
    examples now use `--served-model-name glm-5.1`; weight-table names and
    checkpoint directory names match the download links.
    - Remove the combined-model introduction and GLM-5's historical
    first-supported-version statement instead of applying that statement to
    GLM-5.1.
    - Update the corresponding Chinese translation entries and index labels.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only. No runtime code or inference parameter changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `python -m mkdocs build`: passed for main and releases/v0.30.0.
    Verified the rendered GLM-5.1 page title. Existing diagnostics in
    unrelated pages remain.
    - Markdownlint, codespell and `git diff --check`: passed.
    - Parsed both changed translation catalogs and checked for duplicate
    message IDs.
    - Compared all 33 code blocks with the baseline: only model names and
    checkpoint paths changed. Checked serving shell blocks with `bash -n`,
    confirmed a consistent `glm-5.1` serving alias, and verified exactly
    four GLM-5.1 weights remain.
    - `bash format.sh ci` was attempted but stalled installing actionlint on
    Windows and was stopped. Targeted documentation checks completed.
    - No NPU serving or performance benchmark was run locally.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    ---------
    
